---
/* L50 - accuracy against the base rate. One writer: the figures workstream C. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L50.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a sorting bench with four open bins in a row, where a jointed mechanical arm drops a paper slip into the first bin, which is already overflowing, beside a tall heap of slips on the floor."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L50-fig-title L50-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L50-fig-title">Accuracy against the base rate, and the mistakes behind it</title>
      <desc id="L50-fig-desc">
        On the left, two bars compare accuracy: a plain bar for the always-billing shortcut reaching a dashed prussian line labelled the base rate of 80 percent, and a tinted bar for the model reaching 70 percent, below the line. On the right, a two-by-two grid of small boxes holds the model's mistakes: TP 70, FP 20, FN 10 and an empty dashed box for TN 0. The bars rise into place, then the four grid boxes fade in one after another.
      </desc>
      <text x="40" y="56" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">accuracy</text>
      <line x1="60" y1="210" x2="310" y2="210" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="60" y1="98" x2="310" y2="98" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
      <text x="64" y="90" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">base rate 80%</text>

      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.6s;" x="90" y="98" width="60" height="112" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="100" y="200" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">80%</text>
      <text x="74" y="228" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">always billing</text>

      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.35s;" x="200" y="112" width="60" height="98" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="210" y="200" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">70%</text>
      <text x="196" y="228" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the model</text>

      <text x="360" y="56" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">one model's mistakes</text>
      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.7s;" x="380" y="80" width="100" height="58" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.7s;" x="392" y="114" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">TP 70</text>
      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.9s;" x="490" y="80" width="100" height="58" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.9s;" x="502" y="114" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">FP 20</text>
      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.1s;" x="380" y="148" width="100" height="58" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.1s;" x="392" y="182" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">FN 10</text>
      <rect class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.3s;" x="490" y="148" width="100" height="58" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.3s;" x="502" y="182" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">TN 0</text>

      <text x="40" y="268" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">an average can hide the rare case that always fails</text>
      <text x="40" y="284" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">and cannot see how sure the model was</text>

    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L50</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">The always-billing shortcut scores 80 percent without deciding anything, so a model has to beat the base rate - and the grid behind the score is where the real failures hide.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
